35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the treasurer spent six hours a month chasing individual payments, but only one for yearly collections. That’s a huge difference.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, regardless of attendance. Bank statements reveal a third of renewals needed reminders.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The rota matches the top of the attendance list. The same nine people set up and lock up, carrying the physical load.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,The door charge killed weekday turnout by a third. People stopped feeling those evenings were already theirs.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The sign-in sheets confirm it: a quarter of members account for two-thirds of attendances, while eighteen names appear on no sheet at all.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if seventy percent is fixed, does that mean a flat fee is the only way to cover it without chasing people?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, not the only way, but the most efficient. Chasing individual payments costs six hours monthly; a flat fee costs one.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, efficiency is one thing, but if the same nine people do the work, a flat fee just pays for their absence.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, the data shows people stopped feeling those evenings were theirs once we charged per event. A flat fee restores that sense of belonging.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, the data shows the same nine people do the work. A flat fee doesn't fix that imbalance, it just hides it behind a uniform price tag.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if yearly collection saves five hours a month, that’s a huge relief for whoever takes the job next.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, precisely. The administrative burden is the deciding factor. We cannot sustain a structure that requires constant chasing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shunichi, hiding the imbalance is better than breaking the trust that lets newcomers drift in. We need stability before we can fix the rota.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minako, I agree. The hesitation is real. If we make people pay per event, we lose the casuals who might eventually become regulars.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, stability isn't the same as fairness. If the fee doesn't reflect actual use, the core members will resent subsidizing the absent ones.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, I hear you. If the flat fee saves the treasurer five hours a month, that’s a huge relief. I’m leaning that way now.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, agreed. The administrative savings are decisive. We need a structure that doesn’t burn out the person holding the books.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Shunichi, I hear your frustration, but the minute books show named grades caused friction. We need a structure that lets people drift in, not one that sorts them.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Minako, exactly. The taster forms prove people won’t commit to a whole year at once. We need a low barrier to entry, not rigid tiers.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, the minute books are from years ago. The current resentment is about paying for empty chairs, not old labels. I’m not asking for grades, just honesty.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
